  "names": {
    "order": "given family",
    "conventions": "Given name then family name, often with a middle name. Most Danes carry a -sen surname (Nielsen, Jensen, Hansen) frozen from old patronymics, so many add or switch to a more distinctive name such as Møller, Holm or Lund. First names come from an official list of approved names. Everyone is on first-name terms, bosses and elders included, and 'du' is used with almost everybody. Danes with Turkish, Arab, Kurdish, Pakistani, Polish or Somali roots usually keep family names from their parents' language; Polish women's surnames end in -ska where men's end in -ski.",
